## Project origin

Concord originated from the Code With Antonio "Google Docs Clone"
tutorial (a commercial Next.js/React/Clerk/Convex/Liveblocks course
product). The project was deliberately rebuilt into an original
engineering work: the synchronization stack — the C++20/WASM sequence
CRDT, the Rust sync gateways, the binary wire protocol, the PostgreSQL
durable plane (schema, ingest, snapshots, recovery, history), and the
browser local-first runtime — is original to this repository. The
pristine tutorial baseline is preserved for transparency at the git tag
`antonio-original-baseline`.

The seven baseline template thumbnails and baseline logo have been
replaced with newly authored Concord SVGs; unused baseline starter SVGs,
fonts and favicon were removed. The baseline template copy has been
rewritten. Some product-shell source remains unchanged or modified from
the baseline, including editor and UI components. The path-level
inventory and unresolved review items are in `docs/PROVENANCE.md`.

No official public upstream repository or license for the tutorial has
been identified (tracked as risk R1 in `docs/PRD.md` and
`docs/DECISIONS.md`); upstream licensing remains under review before
any public release or redistribution of this repository.

